Here's a brief overview of the different components and how they fit together to enable full end-to-end pipelines:

\subsection core_modules Core Modules

- **cloudViewer**: Core point cloud and mesh data structures
  - ccPointCloud - Main point cloud class
  - ccMesh - Triangle mesh representation
  - ccHObject - Hierarchical object model
  - ccGenericPointCloud - Abstract point cloud interface

- **CV_db**: Database and entity management for complex 3D scenes
- **CV_io**: I/O operations for various file formats (PCD, PLY, LAS, E57, OBJ, STL, etc.)
- **VtkEngine**: VTK rendering engine and visualization tools
  - Interactive 3D rendering
  - Scene graph management
  - User interactions
  - Measurement and annotation tools

- **Reconstruction**: 3D reconstruction algorithms
  - Surface reconstruction
  - Mesh generation
  - Poisson reconstruction

- **AICore**: Monolithic native AI inference runtime (libAICore, `core/AICore/`)
  - Stable public C ABI under `aicore/` — ggml and GPU backends stay private
  - Quantized GGUF models on CUDA / Vulkan / Metal / CPU, no Python at runtime
  - Task sessions with borrowed image views, typed results and common stage timings
  - Shared model catalog with SHA-256 verified downloads (`asset_digests.h`)

\subsection plugin_system Plugin System

- **CVPluginAPI**: Plugin interface definitions
  - ccStdPluginInterface - Standard plugin interface
  - ccIOPluginInterface - I/O plugin interface
  - ccPclPluginInterface - PCL plugin interface

- **Plugins**: Standard plugin implementations for various algorithms
- **AICore plugins**: 23 AI plugins sharing libAICore — see \ref aicore_sec

\subsection app_layer Application Layer

- **CVViewer**: Standalone 3D viewer application
- **ACloudViewer**: Main ACloudViewer application with full GUI

\section aicore_sec AICore AI Inference

Twenty-three GUI plugins share one native inference library — **libAICore**
(`core/AICore/`), whose ggml runtime is vendored from
[llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp). Quantized **GGUF** models run
on **CUDA / Vulkan (Linux/Windows) / Metal (macOS) / CPU** with **no Python or
PyTorch** at runtime. Results land directly in the DB tree and plug into
reconstruction, COLMAP, and SIBR workflows.

\subsection aicore_abi Public C ABI

Consumers link only `AICore` and include only `aicore/` headers; Qt, STL,
OpenCV, exceptions, backend handles and ggml types never cross the ABI:

- `aicore/depth_capi.h` — Depth Anything V3 depth / pose sessions (`aicore_depth_*`)
- `aicore/gaussian_capi.h` — FreeSplatter 3D Gaussian sessions (`aicore_gaussian_*`)
- `aicore/image_view.h` — borrowed, stride-aware decoded-image input (RGB/RGBA/GRAY/BGR/BGRA)
- `aicore/pipeline_timing.h` — common stage-timing contract reported through `valid_fields`
- `aicore/runtime_capi.h` — idempotent process-runtime cleanup (`aicore_runtime_shutdown`)
- `aicore/asset_digests.h`, `aicore/model_catalog_capi.h` — pinned SHA-256 model catalog and cache resolution
- Per-task C APIs — `yolo_capi.h`, `sam3_capi.h`, `sam3d_capi.h`, `rfdetr_capi.h`, `rmbg_capi.h`, `ocr_capi.h`, `table_capi.h`, `tagging_capi.h`, `relation_capi.h`, `gkd_capi.h`, `vlx_seek_capi.h`, `facedetect_capi.h`, `lightglue_capi.h`, `aliked_capi.h`, `deeplsd_capi.h`, `trellis_capi.h`, `instantmesh_capi.h`, `querysplat_capi.h`, `map_anything_capi.h`, `lingbot_capi.h`, `openpcdet_capi.h`, plus `backend_capi.h` and `inference_log.h`

Each context owns its model/session/cache state; physical backend handles may be
shared through `BackendLease`. Task behavior is configured through options, never
task-local environment variables.

\subsection aicore_plugins AICore Plugins (23)

**Perception — depth, lines, matching, faces, text**

| Plugin | Task | Model | CMake |
|--------|------|-------|-------|
| [qDA3](../../guides/plugins/qDA3.html) | Monocular & multi-view depth, camera pose | Depth Anything V3 GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QDA3` |
| [qDeepLSD](../../guides/plugins/qDeepLSD.html) | Line-segment / wireframe extraction | DeepLSD wireframe GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QDEEPLSD` |
| [qLightGlue](../../guides/plugins/qLightGlue.html) | Sparse feature matching | SIFT/ALIKED LightGlue GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QLIGHTGLUE` |
| [qFaceDetect](../../guides/plugins/qFaceDetect.html) | Face detect / analyze / verify | face-detect.cpp GGUF packs | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QFACEDETECT` |
| [qOCR](../../guides/plugins/qOCR.html) | Text / layout / table recognition | PP-OCRv4 GGUF (EN / JA / CH+EN) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QOCR` |

**Detection, segmentation & open-vocabulary understanding**

| Plugin | Task | Model | CMake |
|--------|------|-------|-------|
| [qYOLO](../../guides/plugins/qYOLO.html) | Detect / seg / depth / pose / OBB / classify + open-vocab | YOLOv8 / YOLO26 GGUF (63 models) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QYOLO` |
| [qSAM3](../../guides/plugins/qSAM3.html) | Promptable segmentation + video tracking | SAM2 / 2.1 / 3 GGUF (39 models) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QSAM3` |
| [qRFDetr](../../guides/plugins/qRFDetr.html) | Detection & instance masks | RF-DETR GGUF (44 models) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QRFDETR` |
| [qRMBG](../../guides/plugins/qRMBG.html) | Background removal | RMBG-2.0 (BiRefNet-Swin-L) GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QRMBG` |
| [qRAM](../../guides/plugins/qRAM.html) | Image tagging & captioning | RAM / RAM++ / Tag2Text GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QRAM` |
| [qRelateAnything](../../guides/plugins/qRelateAnything.html) | Scene relation graphs | RelSGG ViT / ConvNeXt GGUF (24 models) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QRELATEANYTHING` |
| [qGKD](../../guides/plugins/qGKD.html) | Open-world keypoint detection | GKDT-L GGUF (ECCV 2026) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QGKD` |
| [qVLXSeek](../../guides/plugins/qVLXSeek.html) | Open-vocab grounding & region QA | VLX-Seek 1.5-10B GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QVLXSEEK` |
| [qWeVisOne](../../guides/plugins/qWeVisOne.html) | Unified visual perception (11 tasks) | WeVisOne-VL 2B/4B GGUF (Qwen3-VL) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QWEVISONE` |

**3D generation & reconstruction**

| Plugin | Task | Model | CMake |
|--------|------|-------|-------|
| [qFreeSplatter](../../guides/plugins/qFreeSplatter.html) | Uncalibrated photos → 3D Gaussian splats | FreeSplatter GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QFREESPLATTER` |
| [qTrellis](../../guides/plugins/qTrellis.html) | Single image → 3D mesh with PBR | TRELLIS.2 GGUF (DINOv3 + flow DiTs) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QTRELLIS` |
| [qInstantMesh](../../guides/plugins/qInstantMesh.html) | Single image → textured 3D mesh | InstantMesh GGUF (14 files) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QINSTANTMESH` |
| [qSAM3D](../../guides/plugins/qSAM3D.html) | Single image → 3D object | SAM 3D Objects GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QSAM3D` |
| [qQuerySplat](../../guides/plugins/qQuerySplat.html) | 2–16 unposed photos → 3DGS scene | QuerySplat + VGGT-Omega GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QQUERYSPLAT` |
| [qMapAnything](../../guides/plugins/qMapAnything.html) | Multi-view metric reconstruction | VGGT-Omega / MapAnything / Pi3 / VGGT-1B / DUSt3R GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QMAPANYTHING` |
| [qLingbotMap](../../guides/plugins/qLingbotMap.html) | Streaming RGB-D reconstruction | LingBot-Map GCT GGUF | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QLINGBOTMAP` |
| [qOpenPCDet](../../guides/plugins/qOpenPCDet.html) | LiDAR 3D object detection | OpenPCDet GGUF (54 models) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QOPENPCDET` |

**Annotation workbench**

| Plugin | Task | Model | CMake |
|--------|------|-------|-------|
| [qAnyLabeling](../../guides/plugins/qAnyLabeling.html) | AI-assisted image & 3D annotation | AICore catalogs (YOLO, SAM3, RF-DETR, …) | `PLUGIN_STANDARD_QANYLABELING` |

Enable with `-DAICore_ENABLED=ON` plus the per-plugin `PLUGIN_STANDARD_Q*` flags
(see the <a href="../../getting_started/build_from_source.html">build guide</a>).
User guides: <a href="../../guides/plugins/README.html">AICore plugins overview</a>.
Runtime topology and the engineering contract: `core/AICore/README.md` and
`core/AICore/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` in the repository.

\section quickstart_cpp_sec C++ Quick Start

\subsection basic_usage Basic Usage

\code{.cpp}
#include <ccPointCloud.h>
#include <FileIOFilter.h>

int main() {
    // Load a point cloud
    ccPointCloud* cloud = FileIOFilter::LoadFromFile(
        "cloud.pcd", 
        CC_SHIFT_MODE::AUTO,
        nullptr
    );
    
    if (cloud) {
        std::cout << "Loaded " << cloud->size() << " points" << std::endl;
        
        // Process the point cloud
        // ... your code here ...
        
        delete cloud;
    }
    
    return 0;
}
\endcode

\subsection cmake_integration CMake Integration

\code{.cmake}
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.15)
project(MyCppApp)

find_package(ACloudViewer REQUIRED)

add_executable(my_app main.cpp)
target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE 
    ACloudViewer::Core 
    ACloudViewer::IO
)
\endcode

\section python_sec Python Quick Start

Pre-built pip packages support Ubuntu 20.04+, macOS 10.15+ and Windows 10+ (64-bit) with Python 3.10-3.13.

\code{.sh}
# Install
pip install cloudViewer

# Verify installation
python -c "import cloudViewer; print(cloudViewer.__version__)"

# Python API example
python -c "import cloudViewer as cv3d; \
    cloud = cv3d.io.read_point_cloud('cloud.pcd'); \
    print(f'Loaded {len(cloud.points)} points')"
\endcode

